whisper: Lesson 8: When things go wrong
whisper:
whisper: Everyone makes mistakes. Fathom tries hard to tell you what went wrong in plain words,
whisper: and usually how to fix it.
whisper:
whisper: Make one on purpose first. Change "score" on the last line to "scroe", then look at the
whisper: Mistakes tab at the bottom. Click the message and it takes you to the line. Then put it back.
whisper:
whisper: Some problems only turn up while the program runs, like a file that isn't there.
whisper: "try:" lets you deal with those yourself, and "the wound" is what went wrong.
whisper:
whisper: Your turn: run it, then get the plane in the air by giving it more fuel.

to fly, given fuel (a number):
  if fuel falls below 10: raise an error with "not enough fuel (only " plus fuel plus ")"
  scrawl "Up we go!"
and the universe said i love you

genesis:
  set score to 0
  try:
    fly with 3
  if that went wrong:
    scrawl "Grounded: ", the wound
  scrawl "Score: ", score
and the universe said i love you
